163
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:12,240
So it's just like, yeah, you get you have to sus sus the environment.

164
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:12,640
Yeah.

165
00:13:12,640 --> 00:13:13,840
Yeah, no, such a good point.

166
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:17,440
I think that's something a lot of people miss and that I've been trying to talk about.

167
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:34,240
I think Dawson and I even talked about this on the livestream is that, you know, when you see a CalAI blow up and you try and go replicate that playbook and it falls flat, you know, part of it is not understanding the kind of I hate the word but synergies.

168
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:36,880
You're a former management consultant.

169
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:38,320
You can use the word synergies, right?

170
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:47,360
But there were kind of inherent benefits, like you described to CalAI slipping perfectly into content.

171
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:48,640
We're so many apps that.

172
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:51,920
try this playbook don't have that kind of hook.

173
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:53,680
There, there's like layers to it.

174
00:13:54,160 --> 00:14:02,080
It's like creator app fit, like you said, health and wellness influencers with a calorie tracking app.

175
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:24,800
But then it's even that's a step above that is like, is our product even something that can be shown in a compelling way on social that's going to hook someone quickly or even, I mean, part of the reason it works so well too is that the whole video wasn't about, you know, people think they need to make the video a sales pitch for their app, but really by making great content.

176
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:35,200
that happens to mention the app is almost better if it's so compelling that that, like, you know, ten seconds showing CalAI scanning your food is so compelling that people take action.

177
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:41,840
And so it's like there's layers and layers of like things that have to fit together for this kind of strategy to really pop off.

178
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:42,320
Yeah.

179
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:43,440
There's so much to it, right?

180
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:48,320
Like to your point, what we called it was the magic moment and CalAI had a magic moment.

181
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,920
It was like a one, two, three punch.

182
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:51,760
You scan, analyze results.

183
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:56,640
And when you showed that on the screen, people would do like a double take.

184
00:14:56,880 --> 00:14:58,000
They're like, whoa, what was it?

185
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:58,720
Oh, so cool.

186
00:14:58,880 --> 00:15:00,720
Like did that really just calculate the calories?

187
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,160
They had never seen it before.

188
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:04,160
So it was like very impressive to them.

189
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:12,640
If your app doesn't have a magic moment, it doesn't lend itself well to a seamless integration because it's not going to cause that double take.

190
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:13,920
Whoa, what just happened?

191
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:24,880
And if you don't have the double take, people probably aren't going to convert, they may blink and miss the integration and just like, you know, miss the tree for the forest, if you will.

192
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:32,720
And that's like maybe you're better served running paid ads for that where you do like a hard sell and you're really communicating the value prop of your app.

193
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:40,560
Additionally, the magic moment needs to be easily digestible and easily understandable in seconds.

194
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:47,520
It doesn't, it can't have some, it can't require some long explanation of how it works or why it works.

195
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,160
Otherwise, it's going to feel like an ad.

196
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:52,960
And if it feels like an ad, it's not going to go viral.

197
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:55,440
If it's not going to go viral, it's not going to be profitable.

198
00:15:55,920 --> 00:16:02,640
And you all did so many subtle things that I think a lot of people kind of missed that actually helped so much.

